<title>USA: Koch raises U.S. posted crude prices 25 cts/bbl.</title>
<headline>Koch raises U.S. posted crude prices 25 cts/bbl.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Koch said it raised the price it will pay for U.S. crude oil by 25 cents, effective Monday.</p>
<p>The increase brings the new price for U.S. benchmark grade West Texas Intermediate to $20.75 a barrel and West Texas Sour to $18.50 a barrel.</p>
<p>Light Louisiana sweet crude is now $20.75 and Oklahoma sweet is $20.75.</p>
<p>--New York Energy Desk ((+1 212 859 1620))</p>
</text>
